From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO DNS screen
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the Secure DNS settings of Chromium (a switch, two radio
buttons and a drop-down) with the CromIKO DNS screen:

- An animated orbit: the DNS icon glows in the middle of orbits like
  the ring of the mascot, queries go round them and stars of the logo
  twinkle. Off, it is gray and still, and it lights up when CromIKO DNS
  turns on. With "Remove animations" in Android, it stands still.
- A big status ("Protected", "Protected when possible", "CromIKO DNS
  is off") with the provider, and a big switch.
- "Test connection": checks that the provider answers, with waves
  from the middle of the orbit, and shows how fast ("Connected • 42
  ms") or that it cannot be reached.
- The providers as cards that tell what they filter (blocks ads and
  trackers, family filter, blocks malware, no filtering): Quad9 first
  with "Recommended", "Automatic" (the provider of the network) and
  "Custom" with its address field. A card turns CromIKO DNS on with it.
- Everything takes the colors of the theme, so it follows the accent
  color.

It stores the same settings as before, keeps the checks of a custom
address and the notices of managed browsers and parental controls, and
the summary in Settings > Privacy.

